PATCH 528: the eleven [0x6b4] paint-vector call sites patch 521 left at TWO arguments.

Patch 521 established that the `lcall [0x6b4]` paint service is FUN_0000_26a1, which takes FIVE
arguments, and that the asm's `mov bx,<position descriptor>` is the FOURTH of them -- it converted 64
call sites from `(ax,bx)` to `(ax,0,0,bx,0)`.  Eleven sites were missed and still passed two.

This is not cosmetic, and it is not symmetric across the targets.  The call is written through a
`(code *)` cast, so the compiler infers the indirect-call signature FROM THE ARGUMENT LIST: two
arguments produce a 2-parameter signature.  Under gcc -m32 that is caller-cleans cdecl, so 26a1 simply
reads parameters 3/4/5 off whatever the stack happened to hold and, more often than not, still paints
something.  Under wasm the signature is part of `call_indirect` and a 2-parameter signature does not
match 26a1's 5-parameter type, so the call does not paint at all.  That is a native<->wasm divergence
by construction.

MEASURED, on the terrain-azer1 flow with the two sides finally sampling the same simulation state
(see the tick-gate fix in tools/verify.sh):

    native: exactly one blit into framebuffer row 0 --
            [26de] dst=0xa0000 cx=0 col=0 row=0 recseg=0x55e9 srcoff=0x5d260 hdr=07050008
                   src: 19 19 19 19 07 12 0b 19 34 07 ...
            i.e. a 7x5 sprite, and those bytes are byte-for-byte what the native framebuffer holds at
            (0,0)-(6,4).
    wasm:   ZERO blits into row 0.

The 35 pixels of that 7x5 block were the ENTIRE remaining framebuffer difference between the targets on
both AZER1 and SAUDI1 (104 bytes, mission-independent).  The caller is FUN_0000_787d, whose asm is
    787d: mov di,[0x6d34] ; movzbw ax,[di+0x3f] ; add ax,0x380 ; mov bx,0x8eee ; lcall [0x6b4]
-- ax the glyph id, bx the position descriptor -- and patch 517 reconstructed the arguments but emitted
them as `(ax,bx)`.

All eleven sites verified against re_out/fist_dat_image.bin; every one is the same
`mov ax,<id>` / `mov bx,<position>` / `lcall *0x6b4` shape:

    0000:73d4   add ax,0x1470 ; mov bx,0x8dcc      0000:787d   add ax,0x380  ; mov bx,0x8eee
    0000:81e6   add ax,0x428  ; mov bx,0x90d6      0000:81e6   add ax,0x438  ; mov bx,0x90de
    0000:834a   mov ax,0x700  ; mov bx,[bx*2-0x6f9a]
    0000:836e   mov ax,0x718  ; mov bx,[bx*2-0x6f96]
    0000:836e   mov ax,0x720  ; mov bx,[bx*2-0x6f92]
    0000:8bfb   add ax,0x838  ; mov bx,0x9176      0000:8bfb   add ax,0x848  ; mov bx,0x917e
    0000:8dc6   add ax,0x7d8  ; mov bx,0x916e
    1000:8568   mov bx,0x90ae ; mov ax,0x508

After this patch the [0x6b4] sites are 96 five-argument, 20 arg-less and 1 four-argument.  The arg-less
group is a DIFFERENT class (a bare `lcall [0x6b4]` with AX/BX ambient from the caller) and is not
touched here.

